>>
Rule 1 (shape of a tensor at specific dimension must be greater than zero)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= v_2 ≥ 0 ∧ v_2 < ndim(v_1) ∧ shape(v_1, v_2) > 0
>>
Rule 2 (the minimum value of a tensor should be less than the maximum value)
{v_1 : tensor} |= min(v_1) < max(v_1)
>>
Rule 3 (string should not be empty)
{v_1 : str} |= v_1 ≠ ""
>>
Rule 4 (the datatype of tensor v_1 should be either float32 or float64)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype(v_1) = 8
>>
Rule 5 (If a tensor has more than 2 dimensions, its last two dimensions should not be zero)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 1 then shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 2) > 0
>>
Rule 6 (If the tensor dimension is greater than 0, then the first dimension of tensor v_1 should be equal to integer v_2.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 then shape(v_1, 0) = v_2
>>
Rule 7 (if bool v_1 is true, then tensor v_2 should have at least one dimension.)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 then ndim(v_2) > 0
>>
Rule 8 (if a tensor v_1 is one-dimensional, the value at index 0 must be equal to v_2.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int ⊎ float} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 then min(v_1) = v_2 ∧ max(v_1) = v_2
>>
Rule 9 (If the tensor has two dimensions, the first dimension should be greater or equal to the second dimension.)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 then shape(v_1, 0) ≥ shape(v_1, 1)
>>
Rule 10 (Two tensors' total number of elements should be equal)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : ∃j ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) * shape(v_2, j) ≠ 0
>>
Rule 11 (The shape of a tensor must be the same at different dimensions given by integer v_2 and v_3.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : int} |= v_2 ≥ 0 ∧ v_3 ≥ 0 ∧ v_2 < ndim(v_1) ∧ v_3 < ndim(v_1) ∧ shape(v_1, v_2) = shape(v_1, v_3)
>>
Rule 12 (The dtype of tensor v_1 must be different from the dtype of tensor v_2)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype(v_1) ≠ dtype(v_2)
>>
Rule 13 (If string v_1 equals 'true', then boolean v_2 should also be true)
{v_1 : str, v_2 : bool} |= if v_1 = "true" then v_2 = true
>>
Rule 14 (If ndim of v_1 is less than ndim of v_2, then the minimum value in v_1 should be less than the minimum value in v_2)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) < ndim(v_2) then min(v_1) < min(v_2)
>>
Rule 15 (If the first element of the tensor is equal to v_2, then the tensor should have at least one dimension.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int ⊎ float} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 then shape(v_1, 0) = v_2
>>
Rule 16 (if v_1 is true, then v_2 should be smaller than v_3)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : int ⊎ float, v_3 : int ⊎ float} |= if v_1 then v_2 < v_3
>>
Rule 17 (If v_1 and v_2 are not equal, then tensor v_3 should have at least 3 dimensions.)
{v_1 : int ⊎ float, v_2 : int ⊎ float, v_3 : tensor} |= if v_1 ≠ v_2 then ndim(v_3) ≥ 3
>>
Rule 18 (If boolean v_1 is false, then the maximum value in tensor v_2 must be smaller than or equal to 0.)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 = false then max(v_2) ≤ 0
>>
Rule 19 (If tensor v_1 has dimension higher than 2, then int v_2 must be a number between the max and min values of tensor v_1.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int ⊎ float} |= if ndim(v_1) > 2 then min(v_1) ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 ≤ max(v_1)
