>>
Rule 385 (If the tensor has a bool dtype and ndim is less than or equal to 2, all shape dimensions must be greater than zero)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if dtype(v_1) = 0 ∧ ndim(v_1) ≤ 2 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 386 (If a bool variable is true, then shape of the first shape dimension of a tensor v1 and v2 must be equal)
{v_1: bool, v_2: tensor, v_3: tensor} |= if v_1 = true then shape(v_2, 0) = shape(v_3, 0)
>>
Rule 387 (if the product of all shape dimensions of tensor v_1 is smaller than 100, then v_1 and v_2 must have same number of dimensions)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= if ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : ∃j ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) * shape(v_1, j) < 100 then ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2)
>>
Rule 388 (if a bool variable equals true, then the difference between max and min of a tensor must be less than some integer value)
{v_1 : bool, v_2: tensor, v_3: int} |= if v_1 = true then (max(v_2) - min(v_2)) < v_3
>>
Rule 389 (If a tensor has int or float dtype, and ndim = 2, then min value is less than 0)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ((1 ≤ dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) ≤ 5) ∨ (6 ≤ dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) ≤ 8)) ∧ ndim(v_1) = 2 then min(v_1) < 0
>>
Rule 390 (If one of the dimensions of the tensor has a shape greater than some float and if the number of dimensions is even, then the max should be less than 100)
{v_1: tensor, v_2 : float} |= if (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > v_2) ∧ (ndim(v_1) / 2) * 2 = ndim(v_1) then max(v_1) < 100
>>
Rule 391 (If the dtype of a tensor is int and the tensor's dimension is less or equal to 2, all of the shapes must be greater than a constant number)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: int} |= if (1 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 5) ∧ (ndim(v_1) <= 2) then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > v_2
>>
Rule 392 (If a bool variable equals true and the tensor is 2 dimensional, the product of its dimensions must be greater than zero)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 = true ∧ ndim(v_2) = 2 then shape(v_2, 0) * shape(v_2, 1) > 0
>>
Rule 393 (If minimum value of the tensor is smaller than 10 and maximum value is greater than 10, then the dtype of the tensor must be either float or complex)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if min(v_1) < 10 ∧ max(v_1) > 10 then (6 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 8) ∨ (9 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 10)
>>
Rule 394 (if a tensor has less than 3 dimensions, then there must exist an integer that is smaller than or equal to min of that tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) < 3 then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) <= v_2 ∨ min(v_1) ≤ v_2
>>
Rule 395 (If the product of the shapes of a tensor is greater than some float, and the tensor has more than 1 dimension, then maximum value of the tensor must be smaller than 100)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : float} |= if (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i)) > v_2 ∧ ndim(v_1) > 1 then max(v_1) < 100
>>
Rule 396 (if a boolean is true, and the shape of the first dimension of v1 is less than some integer v2, then dimension of v1 must be less than 3)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : tensor, v_3: int} |= if v_1 = true ∧ shape(v_2, 0) < v_3 then ndim(v_2) < 3
>>
Rule 397 (If ndim of tensor is greater than 0, the string variable is not null, then the minimum value of that tensor must be greater than -1)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: str} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ v_2 ≠ "" then min(v_1) > -1
>>
Rule 398 (If the tensor is 2D and if boolean equals true, then the sum of the two dimensions must be divisible by integer)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: bool, v_3: int} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ v_2 = true then (shape(v_1, 0) + shape(v_1, 1)) / v_3 = 0
>>
Rule 399 (If a boolean is true, then shape[0] of a tensor should not be equal to shape[1])
{v_1: bool, v_2: tensor} |= if v_1 = true then shape(v_2, 0) ≠ shape(v_2, 1)
>>
Rule 400 (If the dimension of the tensor is even, then min of tensor must be greater than its dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) / 2) * 2 = ndim(v_1) then min(v_1) > dtype(v_1)
>>
Rule 401 (If number of dimensions of tensor is greater than 1, then product of the shape of its 0th and 1th dimension must be less than the maximum of the same tensor)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 1 then shape(v_1, 0) * shape(v_1, 1) < max(v_1)
>>
Rule 402 (If a float variable is equal to 1.0, then it is not the case that all dimensions of the tensor are of same length)
{v_1 : float, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 = 1.0 then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : ∃j ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) ≠ shape(v_2, j)
>>
Rule 403 (if a tensor is one-dimensional, and its shape[0] is greater than 0, then its minimum value should be greater than a float)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : float} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) > 0 then min(v_1) > v_2
>>
Rule 404 (If a bool is true and max value of a tensor is smaller than zero, the shape of all dimensions must be equal to 1)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 = true ∧ max(v_2) < 0 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = 1
>>
Rule 405 (If a tensor is more than one dimensional, and has integer dtype, its max value should not be greater than a constant number)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) > 1 ∧ 1 ≤ dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) ≤ 5 then max(v_1) ≤ v_2
>>
Rule 406 (if max and min of a tensor are same, then every elements must be equal to zero)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if max(v_1) = min(v_1) then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0
>>
Rule 407 (if tensor is two dimensional then product of the elements must be less than float value)
{v_1: tensor, v_2 : float} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 then shape(v_1, 0) * shape(v_1, 1) < v_2
>>
Rule 408 (If the data type of a tensor is not string, then its max value should not be equal to its min value)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if dtype(v_1) ≠ 11 then max(v_1) ≠ min(v_1)
>>
Rule 409 (If the first dimension shape of the tensor v_1 equals the integer variable v_2, then the minimum of the tensor must be greater than 0)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: int} |= if shape(v_1, 0) = v_2 then min(v_1) > 0
>>
Rule 410 (if the shape of the dimension 0 of a tensor is equal to 1 and data type is int, then its max must not be smaller than 0)
{v_1: tensor} |= if shape(v_1, 0) = 1 ∧ 1 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 5 then max(v_1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 411 (If a tensor is two-dimensional, and minimum element is zero, then there must be at least one shape dimensions that is greater than 10)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ min(v_1) = 0 then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 10
>>
Rule 412 (If ndim of a tensor is not greater than an integer, then the max of the tensor must be less than an integer.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) ≤ v_2 then max(v_1) < v_2
>>
Rule 413 (If all elements of a tensor are same, then the length of a string should be more than 5)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if max(v_1) = min(v_1) then v_2 > "aaaaa"
>>
Rule 414 (if all shape dimensions of tensor v1 equal to 1, and tensor v2 is float, then max of tensor must be greater than the float value)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : float} |= if ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 1 then max(v_1) > v_2
>>
Rule 415 (If there are only 2 dimensions in the tensor, and one of these dimension equals 1, then all shapes of that tensor must be equal to each other)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ (shape(v_1, 0) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, 1) = 1) then shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_1, 1)
>>
Rule 416 (If the tensor is not 1 dimensional and all the shape dimensions are positive, the product of the maximum and the minimum element of the tensor must be less than an integer variable.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) ≠ 1 ∧ (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0) then (max(v_1) * min(v_1)) < v_2
>>
Rule 417 (If tensor is more than one dimensional, then there must exists at least 2 dimensions i and j where shape(i) * shape(j) = int value)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: int} |= if ndim(v_1) > 1 then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : ∃j ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) * shape(v_1, j) = v_2
>>
Rule 418 (If dtype is an integer type, then all of the shapes of the tensor should be less than or equal to the max value.)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if (1 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 5) then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≤ max(v_1)
>>
Rule 419 (if tensor v1 has same ndim as tensor v2, then min(v1) * max(v2) must be positive)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) then min(v_1) * max(v_2) > 0
>>
Rule 420 (if a tensor is a 4-d tensor, then its max value must be greater than any constant number)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) = 4 then max(v_1) > v_2
>>
Rule 421 (if a string is not empty, and the data type is float, then all the shape dimensions of a tensor should be greater than 0)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: str} |= if v_2 ≠ "" ∧ (6 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 8) then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 422 (If the sum of maximum and minimum values of tensor v1 is equal to some float value and data type is float, there must exist some i such that shape(v1,i) > 1)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: float} |= if (min(v_1) + max(v_1)) = v_2 ∧ (6 ≤ dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) ≤ 8) then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 1
>>
Rule 423 (If a boolean variable v_1 is true, and there exists at least one dimension in tensor v_2 where the shape is a positive number, then the dtype of v_2 must either be 0, or greater than 5)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 = true ∧ ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) > 0 then dtype(v_2) = 0 ∨ (dtype(v_2) > 5)
>>
Rule 424 (if max value of a tensor is greater than zero, then there must exist at least one dimension i such that shape(v1,i) > min(v1))
{v_1 : tensor} |= if max(v_1) > 0 then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > min(v_1)
>>
Rule 425 (if data type is an integer and tensor has less than 3 dimension, max value + min value must be smaller than constant number)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: int} |= if (1 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 5) ∧ ndim(v_1) < 3 then max(v_1) + min(v_1) < v_2
>>
Rule 426 (If a tensor is 2D, and max-min is not 0, every shape element of the tensor must be more than 10.)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ max(v_1) ≠ min(v_1) then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 10
>>
Rule 427 (if all dimensions have the same shape and this shape is bigger than zero, then tensor's dtype must either be bool or string)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : ∀j ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_1, j)) ∧ (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0) then dtype(v_1) = 0 ∨ dtype(v_1) = 11
>>
Rule 428 (If there exists i in (0,ndim-1) s.t shape(tensor, i) is not 1 then a bool must be true)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : bool} |= if ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≠ 1 then v_2 = true
>>
Rule 429 (if the dtype of a tensor is not bool and its number of dimension equals some int value, then the max value of the tensor must be less than or equal to some float variable)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : float} |= if dtype(v_1) ≠ 0 ∧ ndim(v_1) = v_2 then max(v_1) ≤ v_3
>>
Rule 430 (If all shapes of tensor v_1 are the same, and its data type is float, then max value of tensor v_1 must be less than some constant.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: int} |= if (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : ∀j ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_1, j)) ∧ (6 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 8) then max(v_1) < v_2
>>
Rule 431 (If all of the tensor's elements are greater than some integer and less than other, then, string v2 must be "valid")
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: str, v_3: int, v_4: int} |= if (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > v_3 ∧ shape(v_1, i) < v_4) then v_2 = "valid"
>>
Rule 432 (if maximum of tensor equals to minimum, and number of dimension is greater than 2, then max value should be greater than integer)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: int} |= if max(v_1) = min(v_1) ∧ ndim(v_1) > 2 then max(v_1) > v_2
>>
Rule 433 (if the maximum element of tensor v_1 is equal to the integer variable v_2, then dtype of the tensor must be integer)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: int} |= if max(v_1) = v_2 then 1 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 5
>>
Rule 434 (If the first shape of the tensor is smaller than int value and that value is bigger than zero, then data type of this tensor must be string)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: int} |= if shape(v_1, 0) < v_2 ∧ v_2 > 0 then dtype(v_1) = 11
>>
Rule 435 (If the number of dimensions of a tensor equals integer v2 and shape of the first element is great than 0, then the float variable max must be greater than min)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : float} |= if ndim(v_1) = v_2 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) > 0 then max(v_1) > min(v_1)
>>
Rule 436 (If string is longer than 5 characters and data type of tensor is not String, then min value of tensor should be negative number)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : str} |= if v_2 > "aaaaa" ∧ dtype(v_1) ≠ 11 then min(v_1) < 0
>>
Rule 437 (If tensor dimension is greater than 0, and bool variable is false, the product of max and min element must be smaller than zero)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: bool} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ v_2 = false then (max(v_1) * min(v_1)) < 0
>>
Rule 438 (If number of dimensions in a tensor equals to int, then minimum + maximum of the tensor should be greater than a float number)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: int, v_3: float} |= if ndim(v_1) = v_2 then min(v_1) + max(v_1) > v_3
>>
Rule 439 (if a boolean variable is true and max value is equal to 1, then dtype of tensor must be bool)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: bool} |= if max(v_1) = 1 ∧ v_2 = true then dtype(v_1) = 0
>>
Rule 440 (if tensors v1 and v2 are tensors and the dimension of v1 equals to dimension of v2 plus 1 then the maximum element must be greater than 0)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) + 1 then max(v_1) > 0
>>
Rule 441 (If the tensor is of boolean type then it cannot have a float maximum value)
{v_1: tensor, v_2 : float} |= if dtype(v_1) = 0 then max(v_1) ≠ v_2
>>
Rule 442 (If a tensor's dtype is an integer or float, then at least a single element must be positive)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if (1 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 5) ∨ (6 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 8) then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 443 (If a string is not empty and all the shape dimensions of a tensor is greater than 1, then max(tensor) should be less than an integer.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : str, v_3 : int} |= if v_2 ≠ "" ∧ (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 1) then max(v_1) < v_3
>>
Rule 444 (if the tensor v1 has more than one dimension and if boolean equals true and then minimum of the tensor must be greater than some value)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: bool, v_3 : float} |= if ndim(v_1) > 1 ∧ v_2 = true then min(v_1) > v_3
>>
Rule 445 (If the minimum of the tensor is greater than some integer, then its number of dimensions should be a multiple of 2)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: int} |= if min(v_1) > v_2 then (ndim(v_1) / 2) * 2 = ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 446 (If shape of 0 dimension of the tensor is not 1, all elements of the tensor must be positive number)
{v_1: tensor} |= if shape(v_1, 0) ≠ 1 then min(v_1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 447 (if tensor has less than 3 dimension and max value greater than 10, its dtype must be float or string)
{v_1: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) < 3 ∧ max(v_1) > 10 then (6 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 8) ∨ dtype(v_1) = 11
>>
Rule 448 (If the dtype is an int, and the sum of max and min of tensor is greater than 0, then number of shapes must be more than 3)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if (1 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 5) ∧ ((min(v_1) + max(v_1)) > 0) then ndim(v_1) > 3
>>
Rule 449 (if a boolean is true, and the shape of the tensor at dimension 0 must not be greater than the shape at dimension 1.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: bool} |= if ndim(v_1) >= 2 ∧ v_2 = true then shape(v_1, 0) <= shape(v_1, 1)
>>
Rule 450 (if all shape dimension are 1 and if boolean equals true, then the minimum element of a tensor must be zero)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: bool} |= if (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 1) ∧ v_2 = true then min(v_1) = 0
>>
Rule 451 (if shape of any dimensions is odd number, then data type of the tensor should be a float, which is encoded as 6, 7 or 8)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : (shape(v_1, i) / 2) * 2 ≠ shape(v_1, i) then 6 ≤ dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) ≤ 8
>>
Rule 452 (if a float number is greater than 0, and all shapes dimension are positive then minimum must be smaller than max.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: float} |= if (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0) ∧ v_2 > 0 then min(v_1) < max(v_1)
>>
Rule 453 (If data type of tensor v1 is integer and number of dimensions of that tensor is greater than 0, then the value of maximum of that tensor must be less than 100)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (1 ≤ dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) ≤ 5) ∧ ndim(v_1) > 0 then max(v_1) < 100
>>
Rule 454 (if the data type is integer and max is greater than 0, there must exists at least one shape dimension of the tensor that is non-zero)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if 1 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 5 ∧ max(v_1) > 0 then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≠ 0
>>
Rule 455 (If the tensor's dtype is an integer type and maximum value is equal to minimum value and greater than 0, then dimension of the tensor must equal 1.)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if (1 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 5) ∧ max(v_1) = min(v_1) ∧ max(v_1) > 0 then ndim(v_1) = 1
>>
Rule 456 (If a tensor is a float tensor and shape of its 0th dimensions is greater than a float number then it should not have any string data.)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: float} |= if (6 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 8) ∧ shape(v_1, 0) > v_2 then dtype(v_1) ≠ 11
>>
Rule 457 (If a tensor is more than two dimensions and minimum value of the tensor is same as maximum value then if that tensor and other tensor have the same number of dimensions, then every shape dimension of first tensor must be same as every shape dimension of other tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 2 ∧ min(v_1) = max(v_1) ∧ ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 458 (if min is smaller than 1 and maximum is greater than 1 then, each of the shape of the tensor cannot be equal to any float numbers)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : float} |= if min(v_1) < 1 ∧ max(v_1) > 1 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≠ v_2
>>
Rule 459 (if the number of dimension of a tensor is not equal to an int, then for all shapes must smaller than an integer.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: int} |= if ndim(v_1) ≠ v_2 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) < v_2
>>
Rule 460 (If the dimension of tensor is less than 3, if the maximum value is smaller than 10, then shape[0] must be greater than integer input.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: int} |= if ndim(v_1) < 3 ∧ max(v_1) < 10 then shape(v_1, 0) > v_2
>>
Rule 461 (If the first shape dimension of a 3-dimensional tensor does not equal the second dimension shape, then the third dimension shape must be positive)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 3 ∧ (shape(v_1, 0) ≠ shape(v_1, 1)) then shape(v_1, 2) > 0
>>
Rule 462 (if the max value of the tensor is smaller than 0, then for every shape, it should be greater than its minimum value)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if max(v_1) < 0 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > min(v_1)
>>
Rule 463 (If the shape of a dimension of a tensor v1 is equal to some integer variable v3, and there exists another dimension that equals to v3, then minimum value of the tensor must be greater than zero)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = v_2) then min(v_1) > 0
>>
Rule 464 (If all dimensions's shape are same, then addition of maximum and minimum of the tensor must be less than float variable)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: float} |= if (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : ∀j ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_1, j)) then (max(v_1) + min(v_1)) < v_2
>>
Rule 465 (if a string has length of five characters, then for all i the value of shape of the first i dimensions of a tensor is less than or equal to the maximum shape dimensions of that tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : str} |= if v_2 = "aaaaa" then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≤ max(v_1)
>>
Rule 466 (If shape of dimension 0 of the tensor must be smaller than a float, and if data type is not of type string, the minimum value of the tensor must be positive.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : float} |= if shape(v_1, 0) < v_2 ∧ dtype(v_1) ≠ 11 then min(v_1) > 0
>>
Rule 467 (If boolean variable v1 equals true, tensor dimensions are equal and first shape is bigger than second shape, then max value must be less than third variable)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: tensor, v_3: int ⊎ float, v_4: bool} |= if v_4 = true ∧ ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ shape(v_1,0) > shape(v_2,0) then max(v_1) < v_3
>>
Rule 468 (If there is at least one dimension with shape greater than some integer, then if bool is true, the maximum value of tensor cannot be same as minimum)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: int, v_3 : bool} |= if (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > v_2) ∧ v_3 = true then max(v_1) ≠ min(v_1)
>>
Rule 469 (if any dimension shape is different, then the min must be smaller than a float)
{v_1: tensor, v_2 : float} |= if ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : ∃j ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≠ shape(v_1, j) then min(v_1) < v_2
>>
Rule 470 (If the number of dimensions of the tensor equals some int, then product of all shapes of that tensor must be greater than that integer)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) = v_2 then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i)) > v_2
>>
Rule 471 (if the tensor is one dimensional and if the dtype is float then all the tensor shape dimensions must be greater than 0)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 ∧ (6 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 8) then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 472 (If a string has more than 2 characters and its first shape is 10, then max value of that tensor must be smaller than 10)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : str} |= if v_2 > "aa" ∧ shape(v_1, 0) = 10 then max(v_1) < 10
>>
Rule 473 (if dimension of tensor v1 equals to dimension of tensor v2 and if dtypes of these tensor are within the integer range then minimum value of v1 must be less than or equal to min value of v2)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ (1 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 5) ∧ (1 <= dtype(v_2) ∧ dtype(v_2) <= 5) then min(v_1) ≤ min(v_2)
>>
Rule 474 (if a float number and a integer variable are smaller than 0, and the data type is bool, then all shape dimensions should equal one)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: float, v_3: int} |= if v_2 < 0 ∧ v_3 < 0 ∧ dtype(v_1) = 0 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 1
>>
Rule 475 (If dimension of tensor is equals 2 and is its first element equal 5 then its dtype must be the float data type)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ shape(v_1,0) = v_2 then (6 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 8)
>>
Rule 476 (if min + max of a tensor is greater than zero, then there must exist at least one dimension where that shape is less than some float)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: float} |= if min(v_1) + max(v_1) > 0 then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) < v_2
>>
Rule 477 (If tensor v1 and v2 have dimensions, and first dimension shape of tensor v1 is smaller than first dimension shape of tensor v2 and v1's data type is integer, then max element of tensor v2 must be less than 50)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) < shape(v_2, 0) ∧ (1 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 5) then max(v_2) < 50
>>
Rule 478 (If number of dimensions in a tensor v_1 is 2, and its minimum value is greater than some integer v_2, then maximum of tensor v_1 must be greater than integer v_2 + 5)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ min(v_1) > v_2 then max(v_1) > v_2 + 5
>>
Rule 479 (If all elements of a tensor equal zero and has number of dimesnion smaller than three , then it should be of float dtype.)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0) ∧ ndim(v_1) < 3 then (6 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 8)
>>
Rule 480 (if a bool is true, and minimum value of a tensor is 0, the tensor's dtype must be bool or dtype is integer and greater than equal to integer variable v2)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : bool, v_3: int} |= if v_2 = true ∧ min(v_1) = 0 then dtype(v_1) = 0 ∨ (1 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <=5 ∧ dtype(v_1) >= v_3)
>>
Rule 481 (if a float value and an int value are positive then any two shapes in tensor must be different.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : float} |= if v_3 > 0 ∧ v_2 > 0 then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : ∃j ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≠ shape(v_1, j)
>>
Rule 482 (if all elements are same, all dimensions length must be 10 and dtype should be a string)
{v_1: tensor} |= if max(v_1) = min(v_1) then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 10 ∧ dtype(v_1) = 11
>>
Rule 483 (if minimum of tensor is zero, if float variable is smaller than 0, then for all shapes must satisfy condition less than integer.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: float, v_3: int} |= if min(v_1) = 0 ∧ v_2 < 0 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) < v_3
>>
Rule 484 (If a tensor has 4 dimensions and the maximum shape of the tensor is greater than the minimum shape, then the data type should be float or string)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 4 ∧ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : ∃j ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > shape(v_1, j)) then (6 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 8) ∨ dtype(v_1) = 11
>>
Rule 471 (If number of shape dimensions of tensor v1 and number of shape dimensions of tensor v2 is 4 and dtype of v1 is same as dtype of v2 then their shape dimensions must be greater than 1.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 4 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 4 ∧ dtype(v_1) = dtype(v_2) then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 1) ∧ (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) > 1)
>>
Rule 486 (If an integer variable and a tensor's dimension are both greater than 0 and shape(0) > 0 then min of the tensor must be equal to the integer)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if v_2 > 0 ∧ ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) > 0 then min(v_1) = v_2
>>
Rule 477 (If the tensor has a string dtype then, the shape of every dimensions of that tensor is not equal to the value of an integer.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: int} |= if dtype(v_1) = 11 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≠ v_2
>>
Rule 488 (If the minimum of a tensor is equal to 0, then every dimensions of the tensor should be less than or equal to 10 if the data type is an integer)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if min(v_1) = 0 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : if 1 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 5 then shape(v_1, i) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 479 (If the maximum value of the tensor is greater than some integer, then if boolean is true, then dtyoe must between 5 and 10)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: int, v_3: bool} |= if max(v_1) > v_2 ∧ v_3 = true then (6 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 10)
>>
Rule 480 (If dtype of a tensor equals to a bool, and its dimension equal to the second dimension, and the second dimension is not zero then if boolean is true)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : bool} |= if dtype(v_1) = 0 ∧ ndim(v_1) = v_2 ∧ v_2 ≠ 0 then v_3 = true
>>
Rule 481 (if a boolean varible is true, then if the tensor is not empty, then the min element in the tensor must not equal to the max)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : bool} |= if v_2 = true ∧ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0) then min(v_1) ≠ max(v_1)
>>
Rule 482 (if tensor v1's data type equals to a string, then tensor v1's number of dimensions must be greater than one)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if dtype(v_1) = 11 then ndim(v_1) > 1
>>
Rule 473 (If a shape dimension of the tensor is smaller than a float variable, then all of its dtype must be equal to a complex number type.)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: float} |= if ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) < v_2 then (9 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 10)
>>
Rule 474 (if dtypes of two tensors are float or complex and all elements for the first tensor is >= 0, then all the values of tensor 2 must be greater than min)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: tensor} |= if (6 ≤ dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) ≤ 10) ∧ (6 <= dtype(v_2) ∧ dtype(v_2) <= 10) ∧ (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0) then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) > min(v_2)
>>
Rule 495 (if two tensors have float or complex data types and the shape of their first dimensions are equal, then the sum of their max elements must be greater than 10)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: tensor} |= if ((6 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 10)) ∧ ((6 <= dtype(v_2) ∧ dtype(v_2) <= 10)) ∧ shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0) then max(v_1) + max(v_2) > 10
>>
Rule 496 (If a boolean variable equals true and shape[0] is greater than 5 and dtype of tensor is integer or float, then min of tensor must be more than 1)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : bool} |= if shape(v_1, 0) > 5 ∧ (1 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 8) ∧ v_2 = true then min(v_1) > 1
>>
Rule 477 (If a 3-dimensional tensor's sum of max and min is greater than a float, then there must exist a pair i and j such that their shapes are not equal.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : float} |= if ndim(v_1) = 3 ∧ (max(v_1) + min(v_1)) > v_2 then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : ∃j ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : (shape(v_1, i) ≠ shape(v_1, j))
>>
Rule 478 (If the shape of first dimension of tensor v1 is greater than integer, and v1's data type is a float, and max is also greater than integer, then dimensions of tensor must greater than 2 )
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: int} |= if shape(v_1, 0) > v_2 ∧ (6 <= dtype(v_1) ∧ dtype(v_1) <= 8) ∧ max(v_1) > v_2 then ndim(v_1) > 2
>>
Rule 499 (If dtypes of tensor v1 and v2 are not same, then ndim of v1 + shape of the first dimension of v1 must be less or equal to max element of v2)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= if dtype(v_1) ≠ dtype(v_2) then ndim(v_1) + shape(v_1, 0) <= max(v_2)
>>
Rule 500 (If a tensor has dimension bigger than 1, then there should exist at least one pair i,j with values in range [0, shape-1], such that tensor shapes values are more than 1, then addition of max and integer must equal to min)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) > 1 ∧ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : ∃j ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 1 ∧ shape(v_1, j) > 1) then min(v_1) = max(v_1) + v_2
